# ProcessCraft Banking: environment variables
#
# The app needs NO environment variables today. It is a static single-page app: everything runs in the
# browser, there is no backend, no API and no third-party service, and nothing in src/ reads import.meta.env.
# `npm install && npm run build` works with no .env file at all, locally and on Vercel.
#
# This file is the template for later. To use it: copy it to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and fill in values.
# On Vercel, set the same names under Project > Settings > Environment Variables instead.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite puts every variable whose name starts with VITE_ into the JavaScript bundle that is sent to
# the browser, where anyone can read it. Only put PUBLIC values in VITE_ variables (a public site URL, a
# feature flag, a publishable analytics id). Real secrets (database passwords, private API keys, signing keys)
# must never be VITE_ variables: they belong on a server (for example a Vercel Function), not in this app.

# Public: the URL the app is served from, for share links or Open Graph tags (optional, unused today).
# VITE_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-project.vercel.app

# Public: turn optional features on or off (optional, unused today).
# VITE_FEATURE_FLAGS=
